__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# runs/ and registry/ are evidence, not build output — they are committed on purpose.

# Claude Code local state (agent worktrees, etc.) — not part of the repo.
.claude/

# The continuous proposer's working files. ALL of them quote the operator's private corpus
# and none may enter this repository until its visibility is confirmed:
#   pool.jsonl              a derived index carrying the nu-strings of the source material
#   proposer.journal.jsonl  the ledger — its `evidence` field is the proposer quoting the
#                           Lean source and repo prose verbatim, which is corpus content
#   corpus.snapshot         the settled corpus itself
#   proposer.control.json / status.json   per-machine runtime state, not evidence
# The COMMITTABLE half is runs/proposer.ledger.jsonl, written by `proposerd.py checkpoint`:
# the same record with every quoted span replaced by its sha256. `evidence` is the only
# field carrying corpus text and it is explanatory — resume needs the directed pair and the
# verdict, which are slot hashes. Leaving the whole journal out cost 737 answered pairs to a
# container reclaim; that was a real loss and splitting the file is the fix, not a
# relaxation of the privacy rule.
runs/pool.jsonl
runs/corpus.snapshot
runs/proposer.journal.jsonl
runs/proposer.control.json
runs/proposer.status.json
